.TH gmcui "1" "2026-08-03" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
gmcui \- WebKit container for the LinuxCNC web user interfaces

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gmcui
.BI \-\-url " URL"
[\fB\-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fIW\fR] [\fB\-\-height\fR \fIH\fR]
.br
.I front-end-name
(via symlink)

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gmcui
opens a single GTK/WebKit window and loads a LinuxCNC web application
served by
.BR stmakd (1).
It is the native-window front end for the web-based HAL and machine
utilities.
.PP
When invoked as
.B gmcui
directly, the page to load must be given with
.BR \-\-url .
When invoked through a symlink, the basename of the link selects a
built-in application profile that supplies the URL path, window title
and window size.  The following profile names are built in:
.TP
.B halscope
HAL Oscilloscope
.TP
.B halshow
HAL Show
.TP
.B emccalib
EMC Calibration
.TP
.B tooledit
Tool Editor
.TP
.B latency
RT Latency test application
.TP
.B linuxcnctop-ui
LinuxCNC Status window (the viewer that bare
.B linuxcnctop
execs into)
.TP
.B classicladder
Classic Ladder editor (addresses the
.B classicladder
instance instead of the
.B milltask
default)
.PP
The server base URL is taken from the
.B GMC_REST_URL
environment variable (default
.BR http://127.0.0.1:5080 ).
Positional arguments are ignored, so callers that pass a file path
(e.g. AXIS embedding hooks) work unchanged.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-url " \fIURL\fR"
Load
.I URL
instead of a built-in profile.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title " \fITITLE\fR"
Window title.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-width " \fIW\fR"
Window width in pixels.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-height " \fIH\fR"
Window height in pixels.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and the list of known application profiles.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GMC_REST_URL
Base URL of the stmakd REST interface (default
.BR http://127.0.0.1:5080 ).
.TP
.B GMC_INSTANCE
Instance name appended as
.B ?instance=
to profile URLs; overrides the profile default (usually
.BR milltask ).

